<title>GERMANY: Mannesmann confirms 1996 profit falls.</title>
<headline>Mannesmann confirms 1996 profit falls.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit			   603     vs 701</p>
<p>    Group income from ord. activities    1,010   vs 911</p>
<p>    Dividend (proposed)			9	 vs 8 DM</p>
<p>    Group earnings per share		 22	vs 21 DM</p>
<p>Mannesmann confirms 1996 profit falls</p>
<p>Group profit by division</p>
<p>	Telecommunications		     947     vs 464</p>
<p>	Engineering				18	vs 278</p>
<p>	Automotive				 185     vs 115</p>
<p>	Tubes and trading (loss)	     92	vs 38 profit</p>
<p>NOTE - Industrial group Mannesmann AG said it expects a further improvement in operating earnings this year. Cash flow improved in 1996, strengthening the company's net cash position to 1.5 billion marks. This leaves it in good shape to make previously announced investments in growth sectors such as Arcor and Cegetel, it said. Today's figures were in line with preliminary data released by the company in February.</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
